    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="f16d9997-bd52-5d08-97b8-8028e6b9713a" activityNameId="1acb95b6-f271-5a6a-b5a4-91aa6a9dc322" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Ventilation system, Bürogebäude Verenastrasse, Baden, special components</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Ventilation system, Bürogebäude Verenastrasse, Baden, special components
Production of special components of a ventilation system for an office building with offices, kitchen, restaurant and car park. The inventory is based on a building with a total heated gross floor area of 7492 m2 and a total nominal air flow of 42500 m3/h, total weight of the components: 2379 kg/Unit, building with a specific air flow rate of 5.7 m3/h per m2 heated gross floor area. Data from call of bid including components for commercial kitchen with exhaust and supply air ceiling system mainly made of stainless steel and aluminium. Stainless steel exhaust air hood for kitchen. No ducts included.;
UUID: bfccabff-3006-33bf-8cf9-7bc4fbb4a938
Materials used for the production. Energy use for the different production steps and for heating the production building. Transport of raw materials to the plant. Estimation for infrastructure of the production site included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Technology, materials and components used for ventilation systems in commercial and public buildings
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2013. Process information partly from 2003 to 2012
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data from call of bids for a ventilation system of a specific building used. Data completed with information from literature and from manufacturers 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_bfccabff-3006-33bf-8cf9-7bc4fbb4a938.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
